// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6530 Add rules for proxy execution via Ntsd, PIX and UE-V AppLauncher
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6530
// Pull request author: AditiNagpure
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Child Process Of PIX Engine Host
// Sigma ID: 25d754af-71d9-45f4-a485-42af98e081f0
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Aditi Nagpure
// Date: 2026-10-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127
// Description: Detects "WinPixEngineHost.exe", the launcher component of Microsoft PIX on Windows, spawning a
//   shell or a common LOLBIN as a child process. Attackers can abuse "pixtool.exe launch" to proxy
//   execution of arbitrary binaries through this signed developer tool. The target process is
//   started by "WinPixEngineHost.exe" rather than by "pixtool.exe" itself, so this rule monitors the
//   engine host as the parent.
// False positives:
//   - Developers using PIX to capture a script host or shell-launched application
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Pixtool/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/1f5bf909d1aed0c116000c632651f0ecc539b2d7/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pix_enginehost_susp_child_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\WinPixEngineHost.exe" and ((FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\cscript.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\mshta.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\regsvr32.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\wscript.exe") or (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName in~ ("Cmd.Exe", "cscript.exe", "MSHTA.EXE", "PowerShell.EXE", "pwsh.dll", "REGSVR32.EXE", "RUNDLL32.EXE", "wscript.exe")))
